  "text": "### Bulletin #3: Account Opening Errors – Reduce by 50%  \n**Date Issued:** 2026-02-01\n**Effective:** Immediate\n**Audience:** Branch Managers, Customer Service  \n**Summary:**\nRecent audit found 15 account opening errors in January (0.5% error rate). Target: <0.25% by end of Q1. Key errors: wrong interest rate applied, missing KYC documentation, incorrect address.  \n**Common Errors & How to Prevent:**\n1. **Interest Rate Error** — Double-check Pricing Guide (PRC-GUIDE-2026) for current rates\n2. **KYC Missing** — Use account opening checklist (confirm ID + address before processing)\n3. **Address Mismatch** — Ensure ID address matches application form  \n**Your Responsibility:**\n- Review account opening checklist before submitting application\n- Have manager sign-off on all applications >£10,000 opening deposit\n- Contact customer if any information unclear (don't assume)  \n**Quality Check:**\n- Before submission: Account Manager reviews for errors\n- Daily: Operations Manager spot-checks 5 applications\n- Weekly: Customer Service Manager audits sample files  \n**Zero Tolerance:** Repeated errors = retraining required  \n---",
  "name": "Chunk 5/13",
  "domain": "banking_risk_governance",
  "prev_chunk_id": "016201b025fb4156a87790b95deecd6b_004",
